examples.question_text:
Describe the modality of each distribution of test scores.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=3mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\begin{scope}
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,6);
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x-0.4,0) rectangle (\x+0.4,4); \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\node at (3,7) {A};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(9,0)}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,6);
\foreach \x/\h in {1/1,2/3,3/5,4/5,5/2} {\draw (\x-0.4,0) rectangle (\x+0.4,\h); \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\node at (3,7) {B};
\end{scope}
\node at (7.5,-2) {Test score};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.5,3) {Frequency};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The dot plot shows the number of books read by students. Describe its modality.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=5mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->] (0.4,0)--(7.7,0);
\foreach \x/\h in {1/1,2/5,3/2,4/1,5/2,6/4,7/1} {
\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.12);
\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};
\foreach \j in {1,...,\h} {\fill[black] (\x,0.45*\j) circle (1.5pt);}
}
\node at (4,-1.3) {Number of books};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The curve shows the distribution of scores on a test. Describe its modality and explain whether the different peak heights affect your answer.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(8.4,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,4.2);
\draw[thick] (0.2,0.1) .. controls (0.7,0.2) and (0.9,3.3) .. (1.5,3.3) .. controls (2.1,3.3) and (2.2,0.7) .. (2.8,0.7) .. controls (3.3,0.7) and (3.4,2.1) .. (4,2.1) .. controls (4.6,2.1) and (4.7,0.5) .. (5.3,0.5) .. controls (5.9,0.5) and (6,2.8) .. (6.6,2.8) .. controls (7.2,2.8) and (7.4,0.2) .. (8,0.1);
\node[rotate=90] at (-1,2) {Frequency};
\node at (4.2,-0.8) {Test score};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Each curve shows a distribution of test scores. Match these descriptions to A, B or C:

a. Unimodal

b. Bimodal

c. Multimodal

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\begin{scope}
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.5,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,3.5);
\draw[thick] (0.2,0.1) .. controls (0.6,0.2) and (0.6,2.8) .. (1.3,2.8) .. controls (2,2.8) and (1.9,0.8) .. (2.6,0.8) .. controls (3.3,0.8) and (3.2,2.3) .. (3.9,2.3) .. controls (4.6,2.3) and (4.7,0.2) .. (5.1,0.1);
\node at (2.7,4) {A};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(7,0)}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.5,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,3.5);
\draw[thick] (0.2,0.1) .. controls (1.4,0.1) and (1.7,2.8) .. (2.7,2.8) .. controls (3.7,2.8) and (4,0.1) .. (5.1,0.1);
\node at (2.7,4) {B};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(14,0)}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.5,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,3.5);
\draw[thick] (0.2,0.1) .. controls (0.5,0.1) and (0.5,2.5) .. (1,2.5) .. controls (1.5,2.5) and (1.4,0.6) .. (1.9,0.6) .. controls (2.4,0.6) and (2.2,2.9) .. (2.7,2.9) .. controls (3.2,2.9) and (3,0.6) .. (3.5,0.6) .. controls (4,0.6) and (3.9,2.1) .. (4.4,2.1) .. controls (4.9,2.1) and (4.8,0.1) .. (5.1,0.1);
\node at (2.7,4) {C};
\end{scope}
\node[rotate=90] at (-1,1.8) {Frequency};
\node at (9.7,-0.9) {Test score};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
